VERDICT on seat 13's S-F7:
  the 164 % case REPRODUCES on my build (got 163.7 % at N=250000, total 659130) and is deterministic across two runs.
  INSIDE the 4N cap: 659130 vs cap 1000000.

  on "unbounded in proportion": the sweep gives %d distinct bands over %d budgets, with
  overshoot %s %% to %s %%. The overshoot is ONE FINAL ITERATION's node count, so it grows with
  the position's branching at that depth rather than with N — which is why the PERCENTAGE is
  largest at small N and falls as N rises, not the other way round. It is bounded absolutely by
  the 4N cap; it is not bounded as a percentage of N.
  PRACTICAL: budget for up to 4N in the worst case, and expect roughly 2x on real game positions.
